---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Half one of the locality precondition the stateful guards were always written
# against but never checked (#971).
#
# `222`/`224`/`226` and their siblings decide by looking for a `parallel()` or
# `parallelStream()` call in the ENCLOSING METHOD. `224`'s header argues the
# over-broad direction is safe, and it is. The under-broad direction was never
# covered: a stream can be parallel without the word appearing anywhere in the
# method that fuses it.
#
#   static long tail(Stream<Integer> in) {
#       return in.skip(100).map(x -> x + 1).toList().size();
#   }
#   ...
#   tail(items.parallelStream());
#
# Nothing in `tail` says `parallel`, so the skip was lifted, folded by `308`
# into a distill carrying a `long[1]` countdown, and `502` captured that one
# array into the single BiConsumer several ForkJoin workers then drive. Measured
# on 20000 elements, the rewritten method returns the wrong size on roughly one
# run in eight — which is exactly the race #715 and #738 were closed to prevent.
# The same hole opens when a method returns an unterminated pipeline and the
# CALLER adds `parallel()`, and again for `StreamSupport.stream(spliterator,
# true)`, which yields a parallel stream without either method name.
#
# So the real precondition is that the stream is created here and consumed here,
# and therefore cannot have its parallelism decided anywhere else. This rule
# establishes it POSITIVELY — a recognised sequential SOURCE ahead of the
# pragma and a TERMINAL behind it, in one body — and stamps `local ↦ Φ.true`;
# `292`'s four siblings revert every stateful pragma that did not earn one.
#
# The mark is a RENAME — Φ.hone.distinct becomes Φ.hone.local-distinct — rather
# than an extra binding, and that is deliberate. A pragma carries a different
# binding set per operator, so a rule generic over all four has to end in a
# trailing wildcard; a wildcard swallows an added binding and the rule then
# matches its own output and appends the mark again, which phino rejects with
# "Duplicated attribute". Renaming the φ closes the pattern by construction:
# `local-distinct` is not in the `or` below, so this rule cannot re-fire, and
# the folds at `307`, `308`, `310` and `314` name the prefixed form instead.
# As in `101`/`142` and `217`, the mark is the way round phino's inability to
# test a binding group for an ABSENCE, and nothing ever removes it.
#
# Both lists err the same way, and it is the safe way. A source or terminal
# MISSING from them leaves a chain unstamped, so `292` reverts it and a fusion
# that would have been sound is forfeited — the cost the issue names. A source
# wrongly ADDED that can yield a parallel stream would keep the fusion and the
# race with it, so the source arms are written tightly:
#
#   * the static factories on the four stream interfaces, which are sequential
#     by construction;
#   * `stream()` on a type directly in `java.util` — `^java/util/[A-Z][A-Za-z]*$`
#     matches `java/util/List` and `java/util/ArrayList` and CANNOT match
#     `java/util/stream/StreamSupport`, whose own `stream(spliterator, true)` is
#     the one JDK factory that hands back a parallel stream without saying so;
#   * the character and line views on a String, which are sequential too.
#
# `parallelStream()` is deliberately absent, and would be harmless anyway: the
# existing guards revert on it before this rule is reached.
#
# Detection stays method-local, like every guard here, but the locality is now
# the point rather than an approximation: a chain whose source and terminal are
# both in this body has no second method able to make it parallel.
name: local-chain-permits-stateful
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-source ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-sop,
      𝜏-sclass ↦ 𝑒-sclass,
      𝜏-smethod ↦ 𝑒-smethod,
      𝐵-source-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-mid,
    𝜏-stateful ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.hone.𝜏-op,
      𝐵-stateful-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-tail,
    𝜏-terminal ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-top,
      𝜏-tclass ↦ 𝑒-tclass,
      𝜏-tmethod ↦ 𝑒-tmethod,
      𝐵-terminal-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-source ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-sop,
      𝜏-sclass ↦ 𝑒-sclass,
      𝜏-smethod ↦ 𝑒-smethod,
      𝐵-source-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-mid,
    𝜏-stateful ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.hone.𝜏-local-op,
      𝐵-stateful-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-tail,
    𝜏-terminal ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-top,
      𝜏-tclass ↦ 𝑒-tclass,
      𝜏-tmethod ↦ 𝑒-tmethod,
      𝐵-terminal-rest
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
when:
  and:
    - or:
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'distinct']
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'skip']
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'dropWhile']
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'cp-dropWhile']
    - matches:
        - '^(collect|toList|toArray|count|sum|min|max|average|reduce|forEach|forEachOrdered|findFirst|findAny|anyMatch|allMatch|noneMatch|summaryStatistics)$'
        - 𝑒-tmethod
    - or:
        - and:
            - eq: [𝜏-sop, 'invokestatic']
            - matches: ['^java/util/stream/(Stream|IntStream|LongStream|DoubleStream)$', 𝑒-sclass]
            - matches: ['^(of|ofNullable|empty|iterate|generate|concat|range|rangeClosed)$', 𝑒-smethod]
        - and:
            - eq: [𝜏-sop, 'invokestatic']
            - eq: [𝑒-sclass, '"java/util/Arrays"']
            - eq: [𝑒-smethod, '"stream"']
        - and:
            - matches: ['^java/util/[A-Z][A-Za-z]*$', 𝑒-sclass]
            - eq: [𝑒-smethod, '"stream"']
        - and:
            - matches: ['^java/lang/(String|CharSequence)$', 𝑒-sclass]
            - matches: ['^(chars|codePoints|lines)$', 𝑒-smethod]
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-op
    function: string
    args: [𝜏-op]
  - meta: 𝑒-local-op
    function: concat
    args: ['"local-"', 𝑒-op]
  - meta: 𝜏-local-op
    function: tau
    args: [𝑒-local-op]
